  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_024: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat; acc=0.619) shows that adding ResNet50 image features to the strong RNA backbone (pca_n2000 + avgpool) yields a meaningful gain over RNA-only (0.591). We also know avgpool > transformer and multiprofile > singleprofile, so those choices are settled. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether the image encoder quality is a bottleneck—ResNet50 is a relatively modest backbone, and a stronger pretrained encoder (ImageNet ViT-L) could provide richer visual representations that better complement the RNA signal. Question: config_029 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings identical to config_024, cleanly isolating the effect of image representation quality. Why this is the best next experiment: The image encoder is a high-impact design axis with no prior evidence in this search; a single-variable comparison against the current best directly tells us whether investing in a more powerful image model is worthwhile, which would guide all subsequent multimodal experiments. This is more informative than testing a minor fusion tweak (concat vs weighted) because the potential performance delta is larger and the design decision is more consequential."
}

